{"chunk_id": "b6afbb8f1b0e", "text": "This section depicts a spectacular phase of the Kurukshetra battle centered on Arjuna\u2019s overwhelming martial skill. Celestial beings watch from the sky as Arjuna releases a dazzling celestial weapon from the Gandiva, his speed so great that no interval can be seen between nocking and releasing arrows. Chitrasena praises the duel between Arjuna and Bhishma, two nearly unmatched warriors. Arjuna cuts Bhishma\u2019s bow and wounds him, forcing Bhishma\u2019s charioteer to withdraw the unconscious elder. Duryodhana then attacks and wounds Arjuna, but Arjuna retaliates fiercely, slaying Vikarna\u2019s massive elephant with a thunderbolt-like arrow and driving the Kaurava forces into panic. When Duryodhana flees, Arjuna taunts him for abandoning royal honor. Stung by the reproach, Duryodhana turns back as Karna, Bhishma, Drona, and others rush in to protect him, setting the stage for an even larger clash.\nArjuna defeats Bhishma temporarily, wounds Duryodhana, slays Vikarna\u2019s elephant, and drives the Kaurava forces into retreat before they regroup to protect their king.\nThemes: heroic duel, battlefield valor, divine weapons, humiliation of Duryodhana, war momentum", "vector": [-0.0117799649015069, -0.008716237731277943, -0.0006994563154876232, 0.01774018630385399, -0.012803437188267708, 0.02943318895995617, -0.024054942652583122, -0.014248338527977467, -0.025620251893997192, -0.03617606312036514, 0.0043949102982878685, 0.011592662893235683, -0.00925807561725378, 0.0038029018323868513, -0.0004166217695455998, 0.009993905201554298, 0.034891705960035324, -0.0026489868760108948, 0.013325206935405731, -0.024188729003071785, -0.01802113838493824, 0.008836645632982254, -0.004749446175992489, 0.026784202083945274, -0.011452185921370983, 0.03764772415161133, 0.010462160222232342, -0.025954721495509148, 0.004097233526408672, -0.010910348035395145, -0.01386035606265068, 0.0028295996598899364, 0.006441854871809483, -0.01709800586104393